Manage the targets a recon scan can be aimed at.

  add <type> <value>     register a new target
  list                   show every target you own
  verify <id> <method>   prove ownership before a scan can start

Every recon scan requires a verified target. Ownership verification
runs out of band (DNS TXT, e-mail link, RDAP, admin-attest, or
self-assert) and is recorded in the audit log.

Usage:
  usulnet recon target [flags]
  usulnet recon target [command]

Available Commands:
  add         Create a recon target (email|phone|username|domain|ip|ip_range)
  list        List recon targets
  verify      Start ownership verification (uses rdap_match by default)

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for target

Global Flags:
  -c, --config string   config file path (default: /etc/usulnet/config.yaml or ./config.yaml)
      --json            shortcut for --output json (overrides --output)
      --output string   output format: table|json|yaml (default "table")
  -q, --quiet           suppress informational output (errors and primary data still print)
      --server string   usulnet API URL (default $USULNET_API_URL)
      --token string    API token (default $USULNET_API_TOKEN)

Use "usulnet recon target [command] --help" for more information about a command.
